# Copy to .env.local (or set the same names on your host) to leave demo mode.
# With everything empty the app runs on sample data and skips sign-in.
#
# Every value here ends up in the browser, so none of them is a secret.
# Never put an API key in a VITE_ variable: your keys (ElevenLabs and the
# rest) live on your Jarvis backend.

# ── Option 1 (recommended): your own Jarvis backend ────────────────────────
# The address of your backend, without a trailing slash. It must answer the
# endpoints in docs/app-api.md under /app/. When this is set, the Supabase
# values below are ignored.
VITE_JARVIS_API_URL=

# ── Option 2 (alternative): Supabase ───────────────────────────────────────
# Only used when VITE_JARVIS_API_URL is empty. See docs/backend.md.

# Supabase → Project Settings → API → Project URL
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase → Project Settings → API keys → Publishable key (sb_publishable_…)
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Older projects: the legacy "anon" key works too. Use one or the other.
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
